            "Compliance with federal safety regulations is completely inadmissible in a strict products liability manufacturing defect action.",
            "Compliance with federal safety regulations is evidence that may be considered, but does not conclusively establish that the product was free from a manufacturing defect.",
            "Compliance with federal safety regulations shifts the burden of proof to the plaintiffs to prove intentional product tampering."
